From 2b0d02375d6902930c48f77120d824ff04de0832 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haofeng Li <lihaofeng@kylinos.cn>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:07:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ksmbd: require exact stream type names

parse_stream_name() uses prefix comparisons for $DATA and
$INDEX_ALLOCATION.  It consequently accepts trailing-character variants
such as $DATAfoo or $INDEX_ALLOCATION_suffix and assigns them the type
named by the matching prefix.

For the two stream types supported by this parser, compare the entire
type component with strcasecmp().  This preserves the existing
case-insensitive behavior while rejecting trailing characters.

Reachable over the network from an authenticated client; these are the
only two callers of parse_stream_name():

  SMB2 CREATE ("file:stream:$DATAfoo")
    -> smb2_open() -> parse_stream_name()

  SMB2 SET_INFO
    -> FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION -> smb2_rename() -> parse_stream_name()

Changing the common parser therefore covers both paths.

Signed-off-by: Haofeng Li <lihaofeng@kylinos.cn>
Reviewed-by: ChenXiaoSong <chenxiaosong@kylinos.cn>
---
 fs/smb/server/misc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/smb/server/misc.c b/fs/smb/server/misc.c
index dcecb6631fe9..a69f34470595 100644
--- a/fs/smb/server/misc.c
+++ b/fs/smb/server/misc.c
@@ -140,10 +140,10 @@ int parse_stream_name(char *filename, char **stream_name, int *s_type)
 
 		ksmbd_debug(SMB, "stream name : %s, stream type : %s\n", s_name,
 			    stream_type);
-		if (!strncasecmp("$data", stream_type, 5)) {
+		if (!strcasecmp("$data", stream_type)) {
 			*s_type = DATA_STREAM;
 			has_stream_type = true;
-		} else if (!strncasecmp("$index_allocation", stream_type, 17)) {
+		} else if (!strcasecmp("$index_allocation", stream_type)) {
 			*s_type = DIR_STREAM;
 			has_stream_type = true;
 		} else {
-- 
